tools.example:
Shift+Ctrl+N, name "dodge & burn", Mode = Soft Light, tick "Fill with Soft-Light-neutral color (50% gray)", OK.

JSX:
var l = app.activeDocument.artLayers.add();
l.name = "retouch";
l.blendMode = BlendMode.SOFTLIGHT;

JSX:
var src = app.documents[0].artLayers[0];
var dest = app.documents[1];
src.duplicate(dest, ElementPlacement.PLACEATBEGINNING);

1. Turn off the eye icons of the layers you no longer need.
2. Layer > Delete > Hidden Layers.

JSX: app.activeDocument.artLayers.getByName("temp").remove();

1. Add a texture layer above the photo and set it to Soft Light at 60%.
2. Add a Curves layer and set its mode to Luminosity so the contrast change does not shift colour.

JSX: app.activeDocument.activeLayer.blendMode = BlendMode.MULTIPLY;

1. Draw a filled rectangle and add a white Stroke layer effect.
2. Set Fill to 0% - the rectangle vanishes but its stroke stays, giving a hollow outline.

JSX: var l = app.activeDocument.activeLayer; l.opacity = 60; l.fillOpacity = 0;

JSX:
var doc = app.activeDocument;
doc.flatten();
var o = new JPEGSaveOptions(); o.quality = 10;
doc.saveAs(new File("C:/out/final.jpg"), o, true);

1. Right-click a type layer > Rasterize Type.
2. Use the Eraser to distress the letterforms.

JSX: app.activeDocument.activeLayer.rasterize(RasterizeType.ENTIRELAYER);
